                <pb facs="0163" n="157" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg157"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic">March 28,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The President objects to stipulation proposed to be added by Lord Kimberley, as
                    it implies a possible violation of agreement by United States. This Government
                    can not consent to a modus which does not embrace paragraph 4 of proposition
                    telegraphed by British ambassador. You can assure Lord Kimberley United States
                    will enact legislation to enforce award on their part before August 1, and the
                    President will not doubt Great Britain will do the same; but, if for any
                    unexpected reason award should not be in force on that day, it is not desirable
                    either party should have the right to denounce the treaty.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
